  "gaps": [
    "The capture contains several programs (tail of the Social and Criminal Justice major, BA in Social Science, BA in Sociology, and openings of AA in Business and BA in Supply Chain Management); this ledger assumes the requested program is the Bachelor of Arts in Social Science. Confirm the intended program.",
    "SSC 101 is both a Global Campus Foundations course and a major course (\"3 credits from the major may also satisfy Global Campus Foundations requirements\"); it is listed once under major so the ledger totals 30 + 36 + 54 = 120 credits.",
    "Global Campus Foundations courses are listed from the standard sequence; the capture states \"Courses may be substituted\" but does not say which substitutions are allowed or which Foundations category each course satisfies.",
    "GEN 101 (and GEN 104 for students transferring under 30 credits) count toward elective credits per the capture; they are not itemized separately from the 54-credit elective block.",
    "PSY 326 requires MAT 232 as a prerequisite, but MAT 232 is not in the captured Foundations sequence or major list; how it is fulfilled (e.g., within electives) is not stated.",
    "Upper-division and residency rules are program-wide, not course-specific: minimum 30 upper-division credits (18 in the major) and minimum 30 credits completed at the University; no individual course is stated as institution-only.",
    "Minimum cumulative GPA of 2.00 required; no program-specific major GPA is stated for this program."
  ],
